    pr_debug("RX Hash fields_mask is not supported - both IPv4 SRC and DST must be set\n");
    return (-EOPNOTSUPP);
}
```
Reason:
The driver incorrectly restricts the use of RSS hash fields in a way that does not allow combinations of IPv4 and IPv6 protocols. This leads to functionality issues when users attempt to use valid combinations involving both protocols.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (ucmd->rx_hash_fields_mask & ~(MLX4_IB_RX_HASH_SRC_IPV4 |
                                  MLX4_IB_RX_HASH_DST_IPV4 |
                                  MLX4_IB_RX_HASH_SRC_IPV6 |
                                  MLX4_IB_RX_HASH_DST_IPV6 |
                                  MLX4_IB_RX_HASH_SRC_PORT_TCP |
                                  MLX4_IB_RX_HASH_DST_PORT_TCP |
                                  MLX4_IB_RX_HASH_SRC_PORT_UDP |
                                  MLX4_IB_RX_HASH_DST_PORT_UDP)) {
    pr_debug("RX Hash fields_mask has unsupported mask (0x%llx)\n", ucmd->rx_hash_fields_mask);
    return (-EOPNOTSUPP);
}
```
Reason:
This added validation checks if the provided RSS hash fields mask contains any unsupported masks. This allows the driver to accept combinations of hash fields that include both IPv4 and IPv6 as long as they are supported by the hardware, resolving the earlier limitations and handling invalid configurations more robustly.

